---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import HeroHeader from "../../components/HeroHeader.astro";
import PublicEmail from "../../components/PublicEmail.astro";
import { apps } from "../../data/apps";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | Made by Kreativ"
  description="Website analytics, local preferences, storefronts, and Android app privacy policies."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <HeroHeader
    eyebrow="Effective 13 November 2026"
    title="Privacy"
    tagline="How this website and its linked services handle information."
  />
  <section class="ptp-section">
    <h2>The website</h2>
    <p>
      This website is operated by Andrei Olaru, trading as Made by Kreativ, in
      Bucharest, Romania. It is hosted on GitHub Pages. Hosting and network
      providers receive technical request information needed to deliver and
      protect the website.
    </p>
    <p>
      We use Plausible for page views, clicks on navigation, product and service
      links, and counts of prepared project briefs, and Cloudflare Web Analytics
      for performance and usage measurements. We do not send names, email
      addresses, search text, payment details, or download contents to these
      analytics tools. Product click properties describe the product, page, and
      button position, not the visitor. The website does not use advertising
      trackers.
    </p>
    <p>
      Service inquiry events contain only the page and a fixed package or
      service identifier. Brief text, budgets, deadlines, relevant links and
      clipboard contents are not sent to analytics. A prepared brief or inquiry
      click is not recorded as a sent email or confirmed engagement.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy">Plausible's data policy</a>{" "}
      describes event processing, approximate location, and daily visitor
      identifiers without persistent tracking cookies.{" "}
      <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/">
        Cloudflare's Web Analytics documentation
      </a>{" "}
      explains its performance measurements. These services have their own
      processing and retention practices; this page is not a claim that no
      network data is processed.
    </p>
    <h2>Your preferences</h2>
    <p>
      Your light or dark theme is saved in local storage as{" "}
      <code>kreativ-theme</code>. This preference stays in your browser and can
      be removed through your browser's site-data settings. You can block
      analytics requests with browser privacy tools.
    </p>
    <h2>Purchases and contact</h2>
    <p>
      When you choose Send Inquiry and confirm sending your details, the contact
      form sends your name (if supplied), reply email, project details and a
      fixed source label through a Cloudflare Worker to Andrei's business inbox.
      Cloudflare processes the request and email delivery; the inbox provider
      processes the delivered message. The endpoint validates the fields and
      rate-limits requests using a hashed network address. The application does
      not log brief contents or save them in a website database or browser
      storage. Hosting and delivery providers may retain technical records under
      their own practices.
    </p>
    <p>
      The email alternative prepares a draft locally. Nothing is sent by that
      alternative until you send it in your own email service. Copy actions
      write to your clipboard only when you choose them. Do not include
      passwords, API keys, payment-card details or confidential customer data.
    </p>
    <p>
      We use inquiry correspondence to discuss and handle your request. An
      internal lead register may record only a random reference, source, package
      and engagement stage; it is not published or sent to website analytics.
      Email content remains in the business inbox. Contact us to ask about or
      request deletion of information you have provided, subject to any
      applicable retention obligations.
    </p>
    <p>
      Gumroad handles product checkout, delivery, payment, and buyer information
      under <a href="https://gumroad.com/privacy">its privacy policy</a>.
      Product links contain campaign labels identifying this website and the
      link position; these do not identify you. A storefront click is not
      recorded here as a completed purchase.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you email us, we receive the information you choose to send and use it
      to respond and handle the request. Avoid sending sensitive personal
      information or payment-card details. Contact <PublicEmail /> for privacy
      questions or requests about information you have provided.
    </p>
    <h2>Android apps</h2>
    <p>
      The website's analytics do not run inside these apps. Their permissions,
      local processing, and optional Google Play purchases are covered
      separately:
    </p>
    <ul>
      {apps.map((app) => (
        <li>
          <a href={app.privacyUrl}>{app.name} privacy policy</a>
        </li>
      ))}
      <li>
        <a href="/privacy/blockshift/">BLOCKSHIFT privacy policy</a>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Changes to this notice will be published here with a revised effective
      date.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
